// EVT stream (ARCHITECTURE §2.3.3). Framing and versioning: see control.proto.
//
// host -> guest: subscribe (first frame, exactly once), event_ack
// guest -> host: event_batch, heartbeat, error
// Any other variant from a side, or a second subscribe, closes the connection.
//
// Delivery: guestd assigns Event.seq (monotonic from 1 per guest boot) and
// keeps a bounded replay buffer of unacked events. On (re)subscribe it
// resends from max(from_seq, oldest buffered); a gap between from_seq and the
// first resent seq means events were lost and is visible to the host.
// Acks are cumulative. Backpressure: when the buffer is full guestd evicts
// AUDITED/ALLOWED events before DENIED ones; heartbeats are never buffered
// (the latest one is always sent). Every eviction is counted in channel_drops.

